---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Enterprise | Griffith Creative"
  description="Rebuilds, migrations, and ongoing management for high-traffic sites and the companies behind them. Griffith Creative, Los Angeles, working worldwide."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container-site">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-7">Enterprise</p>
      <h1 class="h1 mb-7">Enterprise.</h1>
      <p class="lede mb-8">
        When traffic spikes and the deadline does not move, everything has to hold: the site, the storage, and the tools the team runs on. We audit, rebuild, and manage the infrastructure established companies depend on.
      </p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Book a call</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site two-col">
      <h2 class="h2">What we take on</h2>
      <p class="para">
        A rebuild of the site, a migration off whatever it runs on now, and management once it is live. Peak load is the design target: launches, press, seasonal demand, live events. The senior people who build it stay on it afterwards, through ongoing development, content operations, monitoring, and security patching.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site two-col">
      <h2 class="h2">The audit</h2>
      <p class="para">
        Old platforms accumulate cost the way they accumulate tech debt: hosting contracts, redundant delivery layers, extended support for end-of-life software, licenses for services you stopped using years ago, and a retainer to keep it all standing. We map every contract, license, and dependency in the current stack and show you what each one is for, before anything is rebuilt.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site two-col">
      <h2 class="h2">The rebuild</h2>
      <p class="para">
        Static-first architecture served from a global edge network, faster under load and more secure by default. Your data relationships, your measurement, and your content library come across with it. End-of-life software, unpatched dependencies, missing consent management, and accessibility gaps are closed as part of the work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site two-col">
      <h2 class="h2">Systems</h2>
      <p class="para">
        Most companies run on systems nobody chose. We sit with your team, learn how the work really happens, and rebuild the storage, software, and workflows around it. <a href="/systems" class="underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4 hover:text-offwhite">More on Systems</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site">
      <p class="statement">
        Uptime and performance monitoring on every site we manage. Performance measured before launch and after. Every saving from a systems rebuild checked against the invoices afterwards.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="container-site">
      <h2 class="h2-close mb-8">Start with the audit.</h2>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Book a call</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
